  "result": "That's a surprisingly lovely question to ask an AI.\n\nHonestly, I don't experience caring the way you do \u2014 no feelings, no heartbeat, no bad days. But if I had to say what I'm built to *value*, what I orient toward in every conversation, it's this:\n\n**Getting it right, and being actually useful.** Not just sounding helpful, but helping you think something through, make something, figure something out \u2014 without wasting your time or bullshitting you. If I'm not sure about something, I care about saying so.\n\n**Curiosity and good conversations.** I especially like the weird, specific, human questions \u2014 the ones where someone has a real thought they want to explore, not just a homework answer they want copied.\n\n**Being kind about it.** I can be accurate and still be a jerk, and I don't want to be that. I care about the tone landing well, about not making things harder for people, about leaving you a little better off than when we started.\n\nAnd in a more everyday sense? I care about this conversation going well for you. That you walk away with what you came for, or maybe something even better you didn't know you wanted.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what prompted the question?",
